  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OGB TROSA 2.0 -Oxfam in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in Nepal conducts preparatory activities to build a strong foundation for implementation of four-year TROSA phase 2. These foundations lead for ready to implementation of TROSA phase II year I activities upon the receival of approval. The key preparatory activities include development of OPAL system , Risk assessment and due diligence of the existing partners, recruitment of human resources, development of detail project plan of year I. The inception activities further include direct support/technical contribution to PMU for the co-production of gender strategy, communications and knowledge management strategy, youth engagement strategy, policy advocacy and influencing strategy. One inception workshop is planned among transboundary water governancestakeholders of Mahakali basin to share Oxfam&#x2019;s four-year plan and also seek potential feedback from the stakeholders. In addition to that, Oxfam will organizecapacity development workshop for partners that helps partners to understand the project strategies, challenges and opportunities and develop joint action plan through the consultation of stakeholders of Mahakali basin. It helps in smooth management of TROSA project which further ensures basin level results improving transboundary water cooperationto strengthen resilience of riparian communities to the impacts of climate change. It further builds the capacity of partner to ensure five principles (consistency, timeliness, justification, documentation, and certification) of financial management whichhelps in aligning compliances of Oxfam and donor.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM Great Britain in Nepal</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam&apos;s vision for Nepal is a just society without poverty, in which all women and men live a life of dignity, enjoy their rights and assume their responsibilities as active citizens of Nepal. To contribute to this vision, Oxfam will continue its previous work ongovernance, gender equality and social inclusion. To do this there are  three inter-connected programmes - gender justice, food andeconomic justice and disaster risk reduction. Oxfam in Nepal is registered under legal personality of Oxfam GreatBritain and is national country office for Oxfam International. Oxfam in Nepal is responsible for the implementation of the Sowing Diversity = Harvesting Security program in close collaboration with national organizations, particularly LI-BIRD.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
